{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"harness adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is the second axis of a sandboxed run: it decides "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"which\ncoding agent runs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and translates that agent's work back into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" stream\nchunks. The "},{"type":"link","href":"./providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" decides "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"where"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the agent runs; the harness\ndecides "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"what"}]},{"type":"text","value":" runs. Both sit behind the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox()"},{"type":"text","value":" wiring,\nso you can swap a harness without touching your provider or "},{"type":"link","href":"./workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every harness adapter declares "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires: [SandboxCapability]"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" fails\nfast at the call site unless a sandbox is provided via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"built-in-harness-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in harness adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each agent has its own package with curated per-model metadata. Pass the adapter\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ adapter })"},{"type":"text","value":" and run it under any provider."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Auth"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/grok-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok-build"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokBuildText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/claude-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-claude-code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claudeCodeText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/codex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-codex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codexText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CODEX_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codex login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/opencode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-opencode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencodeText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the process env. No "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" flag."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/acp-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP-Compatible"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-acp"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatibleText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMethodId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" skips ACP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authenticate"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The provider is where the agent runs, not how it signs in. The default\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":". Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" when the machine already has a CLI\nlogin. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-report-from-a-harness","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed report from a harness"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want a typed object after the agent inspects the repo, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. Dedicated adapters and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" honor it. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/harnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"harness-output-can-go-to-a-journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness output can go to a journal"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokBuildText"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claudeCodeText"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codexText"},{"type":"text","value":" can stop holding the agent's\nstdout pipe: instead they redirect it to an append-only NDJSON file inside the\nsandbox ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/tmp/tanstack-runs/<runId>.ndjson"},{"type":"text","value":") and tail that, so losing the host\ncannot signal the agent and any later reader can replay the run from byte 0."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"They do that only for a durable run."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Journaling is opt-in, and the opt-in is\npassing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"both"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durability"},{"type":"text","value":" (the snippet above), a\nplain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(sandbox)"},{"type":"text","value":", writes no journal and streams over a pipe exactly\nas it always has. Pass both and forward the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":", whose value the journal path\nis derived from (a durable run with no caller-supplied "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" throws\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DurableRunIdRequiredError"},{"type":"text","value":" rather than minting one nothing can recompute):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { codexText } from '@tanstack/ai-codex'\nimport { memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\n// Single-process stand-ins; ./takeover has the multi-replica wiring.\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\nconst { runs } = persistence.stores\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const adapter = memoryStream(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: codexText('gpt-5.3-codex'),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId, // makes the run's journal findable again\n    // BOTH stores, or there is no journal: this is the whole opt-in.\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox, { runs, durability: { adapter } })],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter } })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The id must be unique per run: the journal appends, so reusing one makes a reader\nstop at the previous run's exit sentinel. Full details, including what you get\nwithout the opt-in and replay against an already-delivered log, are in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Run Journal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencodeText"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" harnesses do not read NDJSON off stdout at\nall, so they have no journal even when a run is durable."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"any-acp-agent-acpcompatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Any ACP agent ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many coding agents speak the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://agentclientprotocol.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent Client Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n(ACP), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pi"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini --acp"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dozens of others"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nFor any of them that doesn't have a dedicated package, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" (from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-acp"},{"type":"text","value":") builds a harness adapter on the spot, the harness equivalent\nof "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":". Configure how to launch it once, then run it under any\nprovider like the built-in adapters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/acp-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP-Compatible Harness"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide for the full\nconfig (typed models, per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", WebSocket transports, permissions,\nand protocol coverage). For which agents you can plug in, browse the official\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP agents list"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the\n"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP registry"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": pick host login or an API key. The sandbox type does not pick this."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": where the harness runs (local, Docker, Daytona, Vercel, Sprites)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Run Journal"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": how a run's output survives the host that started it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./takeover","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Takeover & Detached Runs"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": detach on disconnect, and the three exports a harness adapter implements to support attach."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": bridge your app's own tools into the in-sandbox agent."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Events & File Hooks"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":": stream the agent's edits and activity to a UI."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"built-in-harness-adapters","text":"Built-in harness adapters","level":2},{"id":"typed-report-from-a-harness","text":"Typed report from a harness","level":2},{"id":"harness-output-can-go-to-a-journal","text":"Harness output can go to a journal","level":2},{"id":"any-acp-agent-acpcompatible","text":"Any ACP agent (acpCompatible)","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA **harness adapter** is the second axis of a sandboxed run: it decides _which\ncoding agent runs_ and translates that agent's work back into `chat()` stream\nchunks. The [provider](./providers) decides _where_ the agent runs; the harness\ndecides _what_ runs. Both sit behind the same `chat()` + `withSandbox()` wiring,\nso you can swap a harness without touching your provider or [workspace](./workspace).\n\nEvery harness adapter declares `requires: [SandboxCapability]`, so `chat()` fails\nfast at the call site unless a sandbox is provided via `withSandbox(...)`.\n\n## Built-in harness adapters\n\nEach agent has its own package with curated per-model metadata. Pass the adapter\nto `chat({ adapter })` and run it under any provider.\n\n| Harness | Package | Adapter | Auth |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [Grok Build](../adapters/grok-build) | `@tanstack/ai-grok-build` | `grokBuildText` | Default `'api-key'` (`XAI_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `grok login`. |\n| [Claude Code](../adapters/claude-code) | `@tanstack/ai-claude-code` | `claudeCodeText` | Default `'api-key'` (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `claude login`. |\n| [Codex](../adapters/codex) | `@tanstack/ai-codex` | `codexText` | Default `'api-key'` (`CODEX_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `codex login`. |\n| [OpenCode](../adapters/opencode) | `@tanstack/ai-opencode` | `opencodeText` | `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the process env. No `authMode` flag. |\n| [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible) | `@tanstack/ai-acp` | `acpCompatible` / `acpCompatibleText` | Default `'api-key'` uses `authMethodId`. `'host'` skips ACP `authenticate`. |\n\nThe provider is where the agent runs, not how it signs in. The default\n`authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'` when the machine already has a CLI\nlogin. See [Harness Auth](./auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Typed report from a harness\n\nIf you want a typed object after the agent inspects the repo, pass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. Dedicated adapters and `acpCompatible` honor it. See [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Harness output can go to a journal\n\n`grokBuildText`, `claudeCodeText`, and `codexText` can stop holding the agent's\nstdout pipe: instead they redirect it to an append-only NDJSON file inside the\nsandbox (`/tmp/tanstack-runs/<runId>.ndjson`) and tail that, so losing the host\ncannot signal the agent and any later reader can replay the run from byte 0.\n\n**They do that only for a durable run.** Journaling is opt-in, and the opt-in is\npassing `withSandbox` **both** `runs` and `durability` (the snippet above), a\nplain `withSandbox(sandbox)`, writes no journal and streams over a pipe exactly\nas it always has. Pass both and forward the `runId`, whose value the journal path\nis derived from (a durable run with no caller-supplied `runId` throws\n`DurableRunIdRequiredError` rather than minting one nothing can recompute):\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { codexText } from '@tanstack/ai-codex'\nimport { memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\n// Single-process stand-ins; ./takeover has the multi-replica wiring.\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\nconst { runs } = persistence.stores\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const adapter = memoryStream(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: codexText('gpt-5.3-codex'),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId, // makes the run's journal findable again\n    // BOTH stores, or there is no journal: this is the whole opt-in.\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox, { runs, durability: { adapter } })],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter } })\n}\n```\n\nThe id must be unique per run: the journal appends, so reusing one makes a reader\nstop at the previous run's exit sentinel. Full details, including what you get\nwithout the opt-in and replay against an already-delivered log, are in\n[The Run Journal](./journal).\n\n`opencodeText` and `acpCompatible` harnesses do not read NDJSON off stdout at\nall, so they have no journal even when a run is durable.\n\n## Any ACP agent (`acpCompatible`)\n\nMany coding agents speak the [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com)\n(ACP), `pi`, `gemini --acp`, and [dozens of others](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents).\nFor any of them that doesn't have a dedicated package, `acpCompatible` (from\n`@tanstack/ai-acp`) builds a harness adapter on the spot, the harness equivalent\nof `openaiCompatible`. Configure how to launch it once, then run it under any\nprovider like the built-in adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key',\n})\n```\n\nSee the [ACP-Compatible Harness](../adapters/acp-compatible) guide for the full\nconfig (typed models, per-call `modelOptions`, WebSocket transports, permissions,\nand protocol coverage). For which agents you can plug in, browse the official\n**[ACP agents list](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents)** and the\n**[ACP registry](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/registry)**.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **[Harness Auth](./auth)**: pick host login or an API key. The sandbox type does not pick this.\n- **[Providers](./providers)**: where the harness runs (local, Docker, Daytona, Vercel, Sprites).\n- **[The Run Journal](./journal)**: how a run's output survives the host that started it.\n- **[Takeover & Detached Runs](./takeover)**: detach on disconnect, and the three exports a harness adapter implements to support attach.\n- **[Tools](./tools)**: bridge your app's own tools into the in-sandbox agent.\n- **[Events & File Hooks](./events)**: stream the agent's edits and activity to a UI.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Harnesses\nid: sandbox-harnesses\ndescription: \"Pick which coding agent runs inside a TanStack AI sandbox: Grok Build, Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, or any ACP-compliant agent via acpCompatible.\"\n---\n\nA **harness adapter** is the second axis of a sandboxed run: it decides _which\ncoding agent runs_ and translates that agent's work back into `chat()` stream\nchunks. The [provider](./providers) decides _where_ the agent runs; the harness\ndecides _what_ runs. Both sit behind the same `chat()` + `withSandbox()` wiring,\nso you can swap a harness without touching your provider or [workspace](./workspace).\n\nEvery harness adapter declares `requires: [SandboxCapability]`, so `chat()` fails\nfast at the call site unless a sandbox is provided via `withSandbox(...)`.\n\n## Built-in harness adapters\n\nEach agent has its own package with curated per-model metadata. Pass the adapter\nto `chat({ adapter })` and run it under any provider.\n\n| Harness | Package | Adapter | Auth |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [Grok Build](../adapters/grok-build) | `@tanstack/ai-grok-build` | `grokBuildText` | Default `'api-key'` (`XAI_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `grok login`. |\n| [Claude Code](../adapters/claude-code) | `@tanstack/ai-claude-code` | `claudeCodeText` | Default `'api-key'` (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `claude login`. |\n| [Codex](../adapters/codex) | `@tanstack/ai-codex` | `codexText` | Default `'api-key'` (`CODEX_API_KEY`). `'host'` uses `codex login`. |\n| [OpenCode](../adapters/opencode) | `@tanstack/ai-opencode` | `opencodeText` | `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the process env. No `authMode` flag. |\n| [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible) | `@tanstack/ai-acp` | `acpCompatible` / `acpCompatibleText` | Default `'api-key'` uses `authMethodId`. `'host'` skips ACP `authenticate`. |\n\nThe provider is where the agent runs, not how it signs in. The default\n`authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'` when the machine already has a CLI\nlogin. See [Harness Auth](./auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n```\n\n## Typed report from a harness\n\nIf you want a typed object after the agent inspects the repo, pass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. Dedicated adapters and `acpCompatible` honor it. See [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Harness output can go to a journal\n\n`grokBuildText`, `claudeCodeText`, and `codexText` can stop holding the agent's\nstdout pipe: instead they redirect it to an append-only NDJSON file inside the\nsandbox (`/tmp/tanstack-runs/<runId>.ndjson`) and tail that, so losing the host\ncannot signal the agent and any later reader can replay the run from byte 0.\n\n**They do that only for a durable run.** Journaling is opt-in, and the opt-in is\npassing `withSandbox` **both** `runs` and `durability` (the snippet above), a\nplain `withSandbox(sandbox)`, writes no journal and streams over a pipe exactly\nas it always has. Pass both and forward the `runId`, whose value the journal path\nis derived from (a durable run with no caller-supplied `runId` throws\n`DurableRunIdRequiredError` rather than minting one nothing can recompute):\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { codexText } from '@tanstack/ai-codex'\nimport { memoryPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sandbox } from './sandbox'\n\n// Single-process stand-ins; ./takeover has the multi-replica wiring.\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\nconst { runs } = persistence.stores\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const adapter = memoryStream(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: codexText('gpt-5.3-codex'),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId, // makes the run's journal findable again\n    // BOTH stores, or there is no journal: this is the whole opt-in.\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox, { runs, durability: { adapter } })],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter } })\n}\n```\n\nThe id must be unique per run: the journal appends, so reusing one makes a reader\nstop at the previous run's exit sentinel. Full details, including what you get\nwithout the opt-in and replay against an already-delivered log, are in\n[The Run Journal](./journal).\n\n`opencodeText` and `acpCompatible` harnesses do not read NDJSON off stdout at\nall, so they have no journal even when a run is durable.\n\n## Any ACP agent (`acpCompatible`)\n\nMany coding agents speak the [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com)\n(ACP), `pi`, `gemini --acp`, and [dozens of others](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents).\nFor any of them that doesn't have a dedicated package, `acpCompatible` (from\n`@tanstack/ai-acp`) builds a harness adapter on the spot, the harness equivalent\nof `openaiCompatible`. Configure how to launch it once, then run it under any\nprovider like the built-in adapters:\n\n```ts\nimport { acpCompatible } from '@tanstack/ai-acp'\n\nconst pi = acpCompatible({\n  name: 'pi',\n  models: ['pi-fast', 'pi-pro'],\n  command: ({ model, harnessCwd }) => `pi --acp -m ${model} --cwd ${harnessCwd}`,\n  authMethodId: 'pi-api-key',\n})\n```\n\nSee the [ACP-Compatible Harness](../adapters/acp-compatible) guide for the full\nconfig (typed models, per-call `modelOptions`, WebSocket transports, permissions,\nand protocol coverage). For which agents you can plug in, browse the official\n**[ACP agents list](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/agents)** and the\n**[ACP registry](https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/registry)**.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **[Harness Auth](./auth)**: pick host login or an API key. The sandbox type does not pick this.\n- **[Providers](./providers)**: where the harness runs (local, Docker, Daytona, Vercel, Sprites).\n- **[The Run Journal](./journal)**: how a run's output survives the host that started it.\n- **[Takeover & Detached Runs](./takeover)**: detach on disconnect, and the three exports a harness adapter implements to support attach.\n- **[Tools](./tools)**: bridge your app's own tools into the in-sandbox agent.\n- **[Events & File Hooks](./events)**: stream the agent's edits and activity to a UI.\n"}
